{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1527784-beast-smass-or-pass","id":1527784,"title":"Beast: Smass or Pass","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-02T14:14:00-08:00","id":1527784,"title":"Beast: Smass or Pass","content":"Think of it as a game if you want, or a way to make the circus burn, basically it's a personal evaluation of each example given in the Corebook of BTP, you can make your own evaluation if you want or show some point that I may have missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T14:19:20-08:00","id":1527786,"title":"","content":"First the Hungers.<br /> <br /> Tyrants:<br /> Anakim: We have Jo, a short woman who is pure muscle, she lets people challenge her and then humiliates her opponents by showing her superiority, the challenge is not always physical, it can often be a debate, but the result is usually the same , has a preference for male opponents. When a man crosses the line and touches her inappropriately, she &quot;beats him without leaving room for argument.&quot; Smash<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: Reynold is a health inspector who works for the city, generally he doesn't complain about his work, but sometimes he sees stains from horrible things that happened in the area, in these cases it is when he acts by forcing those responsible to do the cleaning, he doesn't care what was done, he only cares about the dirt that was left behind. I confess that I didn't understand this approach, with supernaturals it even makes sense, but with humans too, I think there was a lack of information. Inconclusive<br /> <br /> Makara: Ari is a cab driver, in short when hunger strikes he picks up a person and leaves him or her in a district where he or she is totally out of place where usually the victim is either arrested or robbed depending on the place, apparently for show them as far out of the water as they are and he stays to ensure that nothing more than tolerable happens. I even like the concept of being out of your element, but the application was just bad and it just makes it look like Ari is an asshole. Pass.<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Ms Blaise is an assistant principal with a pet scorpion that she feeds when any offenders are sent to her room, they are unlikely to be sent there a second time. Simple, vague, but somewhat functional, I wanted to know more about Ms Blaise's criteria for her &quot;conversations&quot;, but... Smash Barely.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Dave started small delivering packages and rose through the ranks of the company, but he wants the top, to be the boss and look down on the city, but he won't be happy to receive this position but to take it for himself. Eh... what to say about that? It doesn't really help. Pass.<br /> <br /> Collectors:<br /> <br /> Anakim: Zwei is a burglar, not the discreet type, he goes in and takes what he wants and leaves, if someone wants to stop him, he can try, but he probably won't succeed. And that's it, man, this example hurts me deeply, because there is another example previously that would fit better, but that's not the one I'm evaluating at the moment. Anyway, it's a good example... of an arrogant villain and cannon fodder, I just don't say it's useless, because he's a good example of punching your problems in the face. Pass, Pass, PASSSSSS.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: Rose collects teeth, she takes them out of a person's mouth if she needs to, but she prefers not to, as it makes a lot of mess, she usually steals them from under pillows, from places where people keep them, or breaks into dentists' offices, she also has vampire friends who like them too much to pull out their teeth, but only most of them. I would change this concept a little, but as it is. Smash.<br /> <br /> Makara: Yin found a hole next to the coast, every day she goes to that place with a plastic bag, something heavy and metal, and comes back at the end of the day without it, one day someone went there to take a look and they didn't go back seen due to a storm. The next time they saw Yin, she was carrying two plastic bags. Macabre, paranoid, good for a chronicle, but not a good character and particularly not very likeable, so that's an idea. Pass.<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Nigel collects old items of historical value and makes them dirty. I would delete the last part if I were going to use it or I would use it another way. I'm not going to go through with it because it's just really disgusting. Pass FAR AWAY!!!<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Anya owns an apple orchard, each tree has a bow, some are red, some are yellow, and some are green. The people who buy her apples assume they are for some kind of identification, what they don't know is that this is a reminder about what she buried under each tree, red for something with blood on it, yellow for something stolen, green for something that has not been touched or tasted. Eh... did she bury bodies or what? Inconclusive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T22:43:53-08:00","id":1527815,"title":"","content":"Serious question: Is the use of a party game whose binary categories are &quot;would you or would you not have sexual relations with this person?&quot; intended as ironic, or is this the same situation that led to McDonalds briefly running <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/todayilearned/comments/ezfzrk/til_in_2005_mcdonalds_had_an_ad_campaign_saying/\" target=\"_blank\">an ad implying a man wanted to fuck their cheeseburgers</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T06:39:35-08:00","id":1527839,"title":"","content":"Although the term is used and maybe even created that way, nowadays it's just a humorous term to approve or reject, or pass or fail, at least where I come from. Basically, if I use &quot;smash&quot; it means I like or approve, and &quot;pass&quot; means disapproval, but I think you already know that. And this cheeseburger guy needs treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:05:16-08:00","id":1527844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1527784-beast-smass-or-pass?p=1527839#post1527839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although the term is used and maybe even created that way, nowadays it's just a humorous term to approve or reject, or pass or fail, at least where I come from. Basically, if I use &quot;smash&quot; it means I like or approve, and &quot;pass&quot; means disapproval, but I think you already know that. And this cheeseburger guy needs treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say if Satchel knew that or not, but I didn't. I've only ever heard smash or pass in a sexual context and only really on TV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T09:37:32-08:00","id":1527848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1527784-beast-smass-or-pass?p=1527844#post1527844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't say if Satchel knew that or not, but I didn't. I've only ever heard smash or pass in a sexual context and only really on TV.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible that this other meaning is something in countries that don't speak English natively, so in this case it was a cultural shock, anyway, I'm not using it in a sexual way, it even seems like I would consider spending the night with a woman who scares children with an insect lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T12:49:57-08:00","id":1527867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1527784-beast-smass-or-pass?p=1527815#post1527815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious question: Is the use of a party game whose binary categories are &quot;would you or would you not have sexual relations with this person?&quot; intended as ironic, or is this the same situation that led to McDonalds briefly running <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/todayilearned/comments/ezfzrk/til_in_2005_mcdonalds_had_an_ad_campaign_saying/\" target=\"_blank\">an ad implying a man wanted to fuck their cheeseburgers</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the term is used and maybe even created that way, nowadays it's just a humorous term to approve or reject, or pass or fail, at least where I come from. Basically, if I use &quot;smash&quot; it means I like or approve, and &quot;pass&quot; means disapproval, but I think you already know that. And this cheeseburger guy needs treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T15:50:27-08:00","id":1527882,"title":"","content":"Predators:<br /> <br /> Anakim: We have Darius, who claims to have been inspired by a werewolf for his method, in short he hunts the victim and when the opportunity arises he satiates himself by breaking some bones most of the time, or with a slaughter if the horror is hungry. Very simple, but functional whether you like it or not. Smash.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: Father Landon, induces others priests to sin and when they confess Landon occasionally makes their crimes public and sees what the church's attitude is, in fact he doesn't care about the punishment. I think this is in the wrong place and I don't particularly like it very much. Pass.<br /> <br /> Makara: Brianna, she attracts people to rescue her then sinks them, but she doesn't drown them, she just leaves them on a nearby coast or beach thinking she drowned, she says it's to teach a lesson. So... what lesson was to be learned here? Mortality? It may be valid, but the execution is poor. Pass.<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Vanessa likes blood and has a hug that causes small bleeds from what I understand, I imagine it's like a shark skin, that being said, she attacks disinterested people and teaches them to value themselves more, if they survive. I think they had no idea here. Pass.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: John Dawson, basically he kidnaps a family member until he makes the others paranoid and desperate so he releases his prisoner unharmed, kind of bad, but unharmed. I'm not even going to comment on the idea, a player would have to develop this, it could even work, but I'm just judging what it does as written sooooo. Pass.<br /> <br /> Nemesis:<br /> <br /> Anakim: Ogre, a beast who bonded with changelings and now he is an executioner who deals with traitors. His creed is that if you have a problem with someone you resolve it, even if it results in blood, but you don't claim to be someone's friend then stab them in the back. I think it was fair. Smash.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: Jess, she hunts down people who have committed unreported crimes, non-consensual relationships, domestic violence, certain things involving children, you get the idea. She does not interfere in the act, but makes the crimes known, a way of giving hope to the victims. This is a case of discussion, like, could she act more directly? Could she stop some of the attackers? Among other questions, but what we have is good enough and I have a weakness at these times. SMASH.<br /> <br /> Makara: Ahmed is married to Patrick who is a Makara Collector, he collects treasures and hides them in the lake and Ahmed punishes those who invade the lake looking for the treasure, in fact Patrick is the one who spreads the rumors. Okay, it's smart. Smash.<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Angela is a lawyer who represents victims of the strong, rich, beautiful and privileged. She doesn't always win, she still needs practice, and she works as hard as anyone else in her position. However, she isn't afraid to use her powers (various insects) to get the upper hand from time to time. It's a good concept that can be used in many ways, Angela can be a lawyer who fights for justice or if you prefer she just follows a troubled ideology, the description is vague enough at that point. Smash.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Benjamin is an acquaintance of Father Landon, when he induces someone to sin, Benjamin enforces the promise they made. He takes them to the heights and gives them three choices: confess, give up their vows or learn to fly and he's fine with whatever the choice is. There's a good idea somewhere in the middle, but it wasn't this time. Pass.<br /> <br /> Ravangers:<br /> <br /> Anakim: Grace breaks expensive cars and enjoys the show. Fair enough, but I wanted something more concrete to use, although if you're not too fond of arrogant playboys this concept might have made you slightly happy. It wasn't my case. Pass.<br /> <br /> Eshmaki: Lester is a mischievous child who throws bricks at the window and writes &quot;YOU ARE NOT SAFE&quot; on the wall. Seriously, a child suggested this concept? PAAAAAAAASS.<br /> <br /> Makara: Naia causes minor property damage that could be mistaken for natural disasters, but when she really needs to indulge, she uses her lair to summon a storm and knock down walls and flood buildings and happily watch the debris float away. It's functional, very forcibly asshole, but functional I must say. Pass.<br /> <br /> Namtaru: Amon likes fungi, he knows different types, like the one that turns insects into zombies or the one that would make anyone run in fear, but the one he keeps in his home could cover and devastate his entire city in days, but he wouldn't , he has friends among wolves and his life is in this city. He made a deal with the wolves, if his enemies invaded his territory he would release his fungi and the wolves would create a spiritual quarantine to isolate an area. It's quite creative. Smash.<br /> <br /> Ugallu: Diana is a killer and she chooses her victims based on two factors, payment obviously, and how many people will mourn the death, or celebrate. The method depends on what she's most into. So... why isn't that the concept of predator? Even so. Smash.<br /> <br /> So the balance tipped more towards the Pass part, even with some ideas in between, that being said, I would like to post my own ideas for examples for the Beasts, if it's not abuse. Besides, there are still other examples in the corebook besides these to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}